WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.100
A kidney cell line does not form synapses.

2
00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:12.940
Yet make it produce one neuronal protein, called neuroligin, and axons that touch it

3
00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:15.140
in a dish act as if they had found a partner.

4
00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:17.200
What do those axons do?

5
00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:20.440
And does the brain need neuroligin to do the same?

6
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:25.560
Each contact in the brain has to say what kind of synapse it will become.

7
00:00:26.333 --> 00:00:28.293
Grow kidney cells under axons.

8
00:00:28.813 --> 00:00:33.593
Where an axon crosses a cell that makes neuroligin, synaptic vesicles gather at the

9
00:00:33.593 --> 00:00:36.993
contact. Where it crosses other cells, they do not.

10
00:00:37.533 --> 00:00:40.673
The axon also releases those vesicles and takes them back.

11
00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:45.513
A dye taken up during release marks the working terminals, so the cluster is more

12
00:00:45.513 --> 00:00:46.573
than a pile of parts.

13
00:00:47.433 --> 00:00:49.733
Neurexins sit on the axon side.

14
00:00:50.533 --> 00:00:53.113
Neuroligins are their partners on the other side.

15
00:00:53.613 --> 00:00:55.953
Now add soluble neurexin to the dish.

16
00:00:56.553 --> 00:01:01.813
It binds Nurexin first, so the axon's own neurexin cannot reach it.

17
00:01:02.293 --> 00:01:04.013
The vesicle clusters are blocked.

18
00:01:04.653 --> 00:01:08.573
So the effect runs through the bond between neurexin and neuroligin.

19
00:01:09.317 --> 00:01:13.317
So neuroligin can do this, on a kidney cell, in a dish.

20
00:01:13.977 --> 00:01:14.977
Call that sufficient.

21
00:01:15.497 --> 00:01:17.637
It is a clean test of one protein.

22
00:01:18.157 --> 00:01:20.737
But a dish tests what one protein can do.

23
00:01:21.277 --> 00:01:23.457
It does not test what the brain depends on.

24
00:01:23.837 --> 00:01:28.357
For that, you need a genetic experiment: take the protein away from the mouse and

25
00:01:28.357 --> 00:01:29.357
look at the synapses.

26
00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:35.107
Mice lacking neuroligins 1, 2 and III were reported to have synapses in normal

27
00:01:35.107 --> 00:01:37.027
number and structure in the brainstem.

28
00:01:37.387 --> 00:01:41.087
But transmission was impaired, and the mice died from failed breathing.

29
00:01:41.787 --> 00:01:45.207
Mice lacking all three alpha -neurexins died soon after birth.

30
00:01:45.747 --> 00:01:50.727
Excitatory synapses were close to normal, inhibitory fewer, yet released transmitter

31
00:01:50.727 --> 00:01:52.787
poorly. Synapses formed.

32
00:01:53.287 --> 00:01:54.287
They worked badly.

33
00:01:54.950 --> 00:02:00.350
So alpha -neurexins and neuroligins are needed for normal synapse function and

34
00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:03.230
maturation, not for forming most synapses.

35
00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:05.330
Many organizers overlap.

36
00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:09.810
A dish with one organizer on a kidney cell tests what that one can do.

37
00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:14.670
Keep the rule. Sufficient in a dish is not the same as required in the animal.
